{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795376300,"nonce":"3nLe2r55/MjBpIf59NmwyWKCmvE=","title":"unresolved_helper test fails when the program exits before the promoter reaches the helper","message":"an_unresolved_runtime_helper_refuses_the_promotion_instead_of_panicking runs test_mandelbrot_small.hl in hybrid mode with hlp_alloc_obj_sized_flags forced unresolvable and requires the refusal to name the helper on stderr. The program runs for tens of milliseconds, so it can exit before the LLVM promotion starts: no compile attempt, no refusal line, test fails with \"the refusal should name the helper it could not resolve\".\n\nSeen once in a full cargo test -p ash run. Forcing the scenario 400 times on a build with the previous beadie missed the line once, and 400 times on a build with beadie 0.4.0 missed it once, so the rate is the same on both and the race is in the test.\n\nFix: look for the refusal over up to ten runs. Every run must still exit cleanly with the baseline answer and no panic, which is the property the test is about.","files":null}]}